<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Tuscarora Nation</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – present (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Iroquoian people of North Carolina who, after defeat in the Tuscarora War, moved north to become the sixth nation of the Iroquois Confederacy.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Tuscarora lived on the coastal plain of North <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-carolina">Carolina</a> along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roanoke-river">Roanoke</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tar-river">Tar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neuse-river">Neuse</a> rivers, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iroquoian-languages">Iroquoian</a>-speaking people among Algonquian and Siouan neighbours. Their language and traditions point to an ancient kinship with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Haudenosaunee</a> to the north. By the 17th century they formed several groups of towns, trading deerskins with English traders from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Towns were led by their own chiefs, with the southern towns under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-hancock">Hancock</a> and the northern under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tom-blount">Tom Blount</a> by 1711. Colonial traders cheated them, slave raiders seized their people, and settlers at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-bern">New Bern</a> encroached on their land. In 1711 Hancock's towns attacked the settlements and executed the surveyor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-lawson-explorer">John Lawson</a>, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuscarora-war">Tuscarora War</a>. Colonial forces with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamasee">Yamasee</a> allies destroyed their stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-fort-neoheroka">Neoheroka</a> in 1713.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Most Tuscarora moved north and around 1722 were adopted as the sixth nation of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Iroquois Confederacy</a>. Many sided with the Americans in the Revolution. Today the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuscarora-people">Tuscarora Nation</a> lives near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lewiston-new-york">Lewiston, New York</a>, and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/six-nations-of-the-grand-river">Six Nations of the Grand River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1600 CE – present (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">North America and Oceania</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.54%;width:8.46%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – present (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hancock, Tom Blount</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Iroquoian traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tuscarora</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a>, <a href="/countries/canada">Canada</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Skaruhreh, Tuscarora</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1813&amp;focus=tuscarora-nation" aria-label="Tuscarora Nation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2270 740 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tuscarora Nation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3048 1164h0M3160 908h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2590 996h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2590 996h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United States. <a href="/atlas?year=1813&amp;focus=tuscarora-nation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

